6,Mixtecan languages,https://grokipedia.com/page/mixtecan_languages,"The Mixtecan languages form a branch of the Otomanguean language stock, indigenous to Mesoamerica and primarily spoken by communities in southern Mexico across the states of Oaxaca, Puebla, and Guerrero. This family encompasses three main branches—Mixtec, Triqui (also spelled Trique), and ...","Mixtec, Southeastern Nochixtlán",Otomanguean
7,Mixtec Culture facts for kids,https://kids.kiddle.co/Mixtec_Culture,"In the Classic period, political power centers shifted in La Mixteca. Old Mixtec states passed on some traditions to new ones. Power was still divided among many towns. In Highland Mixteca, Yucuñudahui replaced Yucuita as the main power in the Nochixtlán valley.","Mixtec, Southeastern Nochixtlán",Otomanguean
8,"(PDF) Tonal association, prominence and prosodic structure in south-eastern Nochixtlan Mixtec",https://www.academia.edu/65314496/Tonal_association_prominence_and_prosodic_structure_in_south_eastern_Nochixtlan_Mixtec,"May 8, 2025 - However a much more satisfactory explanation can be achieved by positing the presence of floating tones which are the result of one of three processes: right-ward shift of underlying tones, loss of CV segments, or the delinking of Low tones. The main focus of this thesis is to account for the tonal association patterns of Southeastern Nochixtlán Mixtec (MXY).","Mixtec, Southeastern Nochixtlán",Otomanguean
